WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:29.360
Oh, when that dynamite goes off, it makes a racket, don't it?

00:29.360 --> 00:33.680
Ah, but gentlemen, that noise is the sound of progress.

00:33.680 --> 00:38.360
Doesn't it make you proud to know that Mayberry's going to have its own underpass?

00:38.360 --> 00:43.360
By jolly boys, those explosions are changing the face of this town.

00:43.360 --> 00:44.360
Howdy, Hodge.

00:44.360 --> 00:46.360
Here.

00:46.360 --> 00:49.360
Oh, well, howdy, Mayor.

00:49.360 --> 00:52.360
Uh, Floyd, can you take me for a haircut?

00:52.360 --> 00:55.860
Floyd ain't back there, Hodge. He's out for lunch. We're all waiting for him.

00:55.860 --> 00:58.360
Lunch?

00:58.360 --> 01:00.360
You know Floyd takes an hour or more.

01:00.360 --> 01:03.860
Says if he comes back to work right after eating, it all goes down to his legs.

01:03.860 --> 01:06.360
Hodge, what are you doing with that goat in here?

01:06.360 --> 01:07.360
Huh?

01:07.360 --> 01:11.360
You just don't bring a goat into a barbershop. It seems to me you'd know that.

01:11.360 --> 01:14.360
Mayor's right, Hodge. You really oughtn't to bring him inside.

01:14.360 --> 01:15.860
Why don't you leave him home anyhow?

01:15.860 --> 01:18.360
Well, I thought he might like it.

01:18.360 --> 01:21.360
And I've been promising to bring him uptown.

01:21.360 --> 01:24.360
Well, besides, I didn't want to leave him home all by himself.

01:24.360 --> 01:27.360
All that blasting's made him awful jittery.

01:27.360 --> 01:29.360
Oh, it'll be over in another day or two.

01:29.360 --> 01:32.360
Animals wandering around all over town.

01:32.360 --> 01:35.360
I am trying to make something out of Mayberry.

01:35.360 --> 01:39.360
Why, with that new underpass, we could be a real metropolis.

01:39.360 --> 01:42.360
If some folks had just stopped turning Main Street into a farm yard.

01:42.360 --> 01:44.360
Now, you just march him out of here.

01:44.360 --> 01:45.860
Well, leave me tell you something.

01:45.860 --> 01:48.360
Folks are saying the main reason that underpass is going in

01:48.360 --> 01:52.360
is to bring the highway past your brother's fill-in station.

01:52.360 --> 01:54.360
That is a lie.

01:54.360 --> 01:58.360
That is an outright lie. May heaven strike me if that's not a lie.

02:01.360 --> 02:03.360
Come on, Jimmy. Come on.

02:03.360 --> 02:05.360
I'll see you, Hodge.

02:05.360 --> 02:06.360
Here.

02:09.360 --> 02:11.360
Come on, Jimmy.

02:13.360 --> 02:14.360
Here.

02:14.360 --> 02:17.360
Now, Jimmy, you stay.

02:17.360 --> 02:19.360
You stay right here.

02:19.360 --> 02:21.360
Look, I've got me some errands to run.

02:21.360 --> 02:23.360
You stay until I get back.

02:23.360 --> 02:25.360
You, that old butthurt.

02:25.360 --> 02:27.360
Maybe now you'll believe me when I try to tell you

02:27.360 --> 02:53.360
that coming up town is no big deal.

02:57.360 --> 02:59.360
What are you doing in here?

02:59.360 --> 03:01.360
What in the world? Get out of here.

03:01.360 --> 03:03.360
Come on, get out of here. What are you doing?

03:03.360 --> 03:05.360
Come on, come on. Get out.

03:05.360 --> 03:07.360
What are you doing in here? Come on, get out of here.

03:07.360 --> 03:09.360
Get, get, get.

03:17.360 --> 03:18.360
Oops.

03:18.360 --> 03:19.360
Oops.

03:49.360 --> 03:53.360
Oh, that's good, Martin. You're getting good on that piece.

03:53.360 --> 03:55.360
Well, I've been working on it at night.

03:55.360 --> 03:56.360
That's good.

03:56.360 --> 03:58.360
Any phone calls?

03:58.360 --> 04:00.360
No, just old Mrs. Vickers.

04:00.360 --> 04:05.360
Every time a blast goes off, she calls asking if it's Yankee cannons coming down the road.

04:11.360 --> 04:13.360
Sheriff's office.

04:14.360 --> 04:16.360
Yes, Mrs. Vickers.

04:16.360 --> 04:19.360
No, ma'am, that's just Blaston on the underpass.

04:20.360 --> 04:23.360
Yes, ma'am, we're still holding on to Richmond.

04:25.360 --> 04:27.360
I don't believe I convinced her.

04:27.360 --> 04:28.360
Yeah.

04:28.360 --> 04:29.360
Poor old soul.

04:29.360 --> 04:30.360
Yeah.

04:31.360 --> 04:32.360
Sheriff.

04:32.360 --> 04:34.360
Sheriff, he's gone, he's gone.

04:34.360 --> 04:35.360
Who's gone?

04:35.360 --> 04:36.360
Jimmy, my goat.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.360
I left him out front and told him to stay put,

04:38.360 --> 04:40.360
and when I got back, he's gone.

04:40.360 --> 04:42.360
I can't imagine where he's gone to.

04:42.360 --> 04:44.360
Well, he was in here just a minute ago.

04:44.360 --> 04:46.360
Jimmy was here?

04:46.360 --> 04:47.360
I'll be doled, Barney.

04:47.360 --> 04:49.360
Must have liked your French harp playing.

04:49.360 --> 04:51.360
Come on, he must be in the neighborhood somewhere.

05:02.360 --> 05:05.360
Why don't you go around that way, and me and Barney will check up through the alley.

05:05.360 --> 05:07.360
Well, I sure hope he don't do no damage.

05:07.360 --> 05:14.360
You know, that fool goat will eat anything he can get his teeth into.

05:32.360 --> 05:34.360
See anything, Andy?

05:34.360 --> 05:37.360
No.

05:39.360 --> 05:41.360
Hey, Otis.

05:41.360 --> 05:43.360
Listen, maybe you can help us.

05:43.360 --> 05:44.360
Oh, I'm afraid not.

05:44.360 --> 05:46.360
What would I know about anybody selling moonshine, huh?

05:46.360 --> 05:48.360
I'm not looking for a steal, Otis.

05:48.360 --> 05:50.360
Well, what with all the explosions going on, I was out getting some tranquilizers.

05:50.360 --> 05:51.360
You're not.

05:51.360 --> 05:53.360
No, we're not, Otis.

05:53.360 --> 05:56.360
Have you seen a big billy goat, gray hair, with long white whiskers?

05:56.360 --> 05:58.360
Oh, no, no, I haven't seen anything like that.

05:58.360 --> 06:00.360
But I will.

06:00.360 --> 06:04.360
I will.

06:04.360 --> 06:07.360
Hey!

06:26.360 --> 06:29.360
Well, you check the back of the store.

06:29.360 --> 06:31.360
I'll check the other end of the alley.

06:31.360 --> 06:33.360
Think you might have gone in this shed?

06:33.360 --> 06:34.360
I don't know.

06:34.360 --> 06:36.360
We'll take a look.

06:36.360 --> 06:39.360
Jimmy?

06:39.360 --> 07:04.360
You in here, Jimmy?

07:09.360 --> 07:12.360
Jimmy?

07:33.360 --> 07:34.360
What's the matter, Barnes?

07:34.360 --> 07:50.360
Nothing.

07:50.360 --> 07:52.360
Look at that.

07:52.360 --> 07:53.360
What's that?

07:53.360 --> 07:55.360
That's Jimmy's rope.

07:55.360 --> 07:57.360
He's been here all right.

07:57.360 --> 07:59.360
He has?

07:59.360 --> 08:02.360
Yeah, what's more, he had lunch here.

08:02.360 --> 08:04.360
He had lunch?

08:04.360 --> 08:07.360
You mean he ate dynamite?

08:07.360 --> 08:11.360
I'd said he'd eat about anything, and he sure did.

08:11.360 --> 08:19.360
And are you saying that...

08:19.360 --> 08:32.360
Somewhere wandering loose around Mayberry is a loaded goat?

08:32.360 --> 08:34.360
A goat full of dynamite?

08:34.360 --> 08:36.360
What are we gonna do?

08:36.360 --> 08:39.360
Well, the main thing is to stay calm.

08:39.360 --> 08:40.360
That's right.

08:40.360 --> 08:41.360
Nothing to worry about.

08:41.360 --> 08:43.360
No sense getting in a panic.

08:43.360 --> 08:46.360
Just stay calm and cool.

08:46.360 --> 08:49.360
Here he goes!

08:49.360 --> 08:51.360
That's just blasting on the highway.

08:51.360 --> 08:55.360
Now, remember, when we do catch up with him, easy does it.

08:55.360 --> 09:00.360
Treat him extra gentle.

09:00.360 --> 09:01.360
Jimmy!

09:01.360 --> 09:02.360
Hey, hey, Jimmy!

09:02.360 --> 09:05.360
Jimmy!

09:05.360 --> 09:07.360
What is the matter with you?

09:07.360 --> 09:10.360
I ain't ever gonna bring you uptown again.

09:10.360 --> 09:17.360
Oh, I hate to do this, but I am going to give you a good kick just to teach you a lesson.

09:17.360 --> 09:19.360
Hush!

09:19.360 --> 09:20.360
Don't kick the goat.

09:20.360 --> 09:21.360
Huh?

09:21.360 --> 09:23.360
That goat ate himself full of dynamite.

09:23.360 --> 09:24.360
Dynamite?

09:24.360 --> 09:27.360
Yeah, one swift kick and blew it.

09:27.360 --> 09:30.360
Barney, go up to the highway crew and bring back their blasting engineer.

09:30.360 --> 09:34.360
Maybe he can help us.

09:34.360 --> 09:36.360
Eatin' dynamite.

09:36.360 --> 09:38.360
Now, ain't that the way it always is.

09:38.360 --> 09:48.360
First time he comes uptown, he figures he's got to do everything.

09:48.360 --> 09:54.360
Well, I gotta admit, Sheriff, sure a new one on me.

09:54.360 --> 09:57.360
Hey, you better put that on.

09:57.360 --> 09:59.360
You got any idea how much dynamite's in him?

09:59.360 --> 10:01.360
Oh, probably quite a bit.

10:01.360 --> 10:03.360
He's got a very healthy appetite.

10:03.360 --> 10:05.360
What am I gonna do?

10:05.360 --> 10:08.360
Well, looks like you are doing about all you can do.

10:08.360 --> 10:10.360
The more hay he eats, the better.

10:10.360 --> 10:14.360
It could kinda cushion his insides.

10:14.360 --> 10:18.360
You think he could go off?

10:18.360 --> 10:21.360
Friend, I've been working with explosives for 20 years,

10:21.360 --> 10:24.360
and I've learned there's only one thing you can be sure of,

10:24.360 --> 10:30.360
and that's that there's nothing you can be sure of.

10:30.360 --> 10:34.360
Good day, gentlemen.

10:34.360 --> 10:36.360
Stop smoking!

10:36.360 --> 10:39.360
What's the matter with you? Are you crazy?

10:39.360 --> 10:44.360
That goat in there ate himself full of dynamite.

10:44.360 --> 10:45.360
Dynamite?

10:45.360 --> 10:50.360
So no smoking or open fires or radio transmission within 100 feet.

10:50.360 --> 10:54.360
Dynamite?

10:54.360 --> 10:56.360
A goat full of dynamite?

10:56.360 --> 10:58.360
Mm-hmm. And lots of it.

10:58.360 --> 11:01.360
He has always had a good appetite.

11:01.360 --> 11:05.360
Why don't you just pick him up and just throw him out of town?

11:05.360 --> 11:07.360
No, we can't do that, Mayor.

11:07.360 --> 11:10.360
Safer thing is just not jostling. Keep him extra quiet.

11:10.360 --> 11:14.360
Yeah, one wrong move and everything goes bluey.

11:14.360 --> 11:20.360
Is it possible I... I mean, could a goat... bluey?

11:20.360 --> 11:22.360
Mr. Burton here says anything's possible.

11:22.360 --> 11:24.360
Oh, my.

11:24.360 --> 11:25.360
Anything more we can do?

11:25.360 --> 11:28.360
Anything. Anything at all.

11:28.360 --> 11:31.360
Well, to prevent any chain reaction, we could stop our blasting.

11:31.360 --> 11:33.360
But that would delay the underpass.

11:33.360 --> 11:40.360
And I promised my brother it'd be finished by...

11:40.360 --> 11:43.360
All right, all right. Stop the blasting.

11:43.360 --> 11:46.360
What would happen if the goat did go off?

11:46.360 --> 11:48.360
Well, these walls are pretty thick.

11:48.360 --> 11:51.360
Most of the destructive force would go straight up.

11:51.360 --> 11:54.360
Straight up? But my office is up there.

11:54.360 --> 12:02.360
There's nothing else I can tell you, Sheriff. I'll have to be getting back.

12:02.360 --> 12:06.360
I'd better evacuate some of my important papers.

12:06.360 --> 12:08.360
But I'll tell you what ought to be done.

12:08.360 --> 12:11.360
That animal should be destroyed immediately.

12:11.360 --> 12:13.360
How would you propose we do that?

12:13.360 --> 12:16.360
You've got a lot of guns here. Shoot him.

12:16.360 --> 12:20.360
Shoot him. Shoot him. With a gun.

12:20.360 --> 12:27.360
All right.

12:27.360 --> 12:29.360
There you are, Mayor. You do it.

12:29.360 --> 12:31.360
You do it.

12:31.360 --> 12:32.360
Oh, but I... I... I...

12:32.360 --> 12:35.360
Mayor, when you shoot that goat, he's gonna fall down, ain't he?

12:35.360 --> 12:36.360
Yes.

12:36.360 --> 12:40.360
And when he falls down, being full of dynamite, what's gonna happen?

12:40.360 --> 12:42.360
Blew it.

12:42.360 --> 12:44.360
So long, Mayor.

12:44.360 --> 12:48.360
Well, uh... Well, I...

12:48.360 --> 12:51.360
Surely there must be a more humane way of doing this.

12:51.360 --> 12:54.360
But in the interest of public safety, I want that goat out of here.

12:54.360 --> 13:00.360
I want him out of this town.

13:00.360 --> 13:02.360
What are you gonna do, Sheriff?

13:02.360 --> 13:04.360
Jimmy didn't mean no harm.

13:04.360 --> 13:08.360
Like I say, he's got a healthy appetite, that's all.

13:08.360 --> 13:10.360
Hate to see anything happen to him.

13:10.360 --> 13:13.360
He's been like a friend to me.

13:13.360 --> 13:15.360
You better go on home, Hodge.

13:15.360 --> 13:18.360
Leave it to us. We'll try to think of something.

13:18.360 --> 13:28.360
All right.

13:28.360 --> 13:30.360
What are you gonna do, then?

13:30.360 --> 13:33.360
I don't know.

13:33.360 --> 13:37.360
I suspect the Mayor is right, though.

13:37.360 --> 13:40.360
We got to get him out of town.

13:40.360 --> 13:44.360
I sure don't know how.

13:44.360 --> 13:49.360
We'll just have to gentle him out.

13:49.360 --> 13:52.360
I'm gonna go get some more hay.

13:52.360 --> 14:11.360
You come on, too, and get some more pillows and things to pad the place.

14:11.360 --> 14:22.360
Gunkeeper! Gunkeeper! Gunkeeper!

14:22.360 --> 14:35.360
What if it's a holiday?

14:35.360 --> 14:41.360
If it is, I'll get a little rest.

14:41.360 --> 14:46.360
It'll make me feel much better.

14:46.360 --> 15:06.360
I'll get a little rest. I'll get a little rest.

15:06.360 --> 15:21.360
Oh, boy. This is gonna feel so good.

15:21.360 --> 15:41.360
I'm gonna be sleepy.

15:41.360 --> 16:07.360
That's a new one. First time I ever fell off a bed under the wall.

16:07.360 --> 16:23.360
I think I'll just wait for the world to turn around a little more.

16:23.360 --> 16:33.360
Uncle Nat? What are you doing here?

16:33.360 --> 16:38.360
What are you doing here, Uncle Nat? You're a goat.

16:38.360 --> 16:42.360
What are you doing here, anyway?

16:42.360 --> 16:50.360
Okay, this is my cell, and I don't share my cell with anybody.

16:50.360 --> 16:55.360
I don't care. This is a decent place of detention.

16:55.360 --> 17:04.360
It's not a menagerie. If you want to go to the menagerie, then you get in.

17:04.360 --> 17:11.360
All right, pal. Two inches low.

17:11.360 --> 17:19.360
He looks mad.

17:19.360 --> 17:22.360
Watch out, Andy.

17:22.360 --> 17:37.360
Otis, what did you do? That's a mad goat.

17:37.360 --> 17:39.360
What did you do, Otis?

17:39.360 --> 17:46.360
He's in my cell, Andy. What is this, the Middle Ages? Impounding human beings with animals?

17:46.360 --> 17:50.360
That goat's a dangerous weapon. He's full of dynamite.

17:50.360 --> 17:54.360
Huh? Yes, he ate a case of dynamite. You wouldn't have to show up today, Otis.

17:54.360 --> 17:58.360
About one loaded goat at a time is all we can handle.

17:58.360 --> 18:16.360
Dynamite? That goat's filled with...

18:16.360 --> 18:17.360
What happened?

18:17.360 --> 18:20.360
Oh, I just kicked him out of the cell and he got mad.

18:20.360 --> 18:23.360
Well, why didn't somebody tell me? Why didn't somebody give me warning?

18:23.360 --> 18:26.360
Why didn't you tie something red on his tail? That way he'd...

18:26.360 --> 18:28.360
Oh, shut up, Otis. Just shut up.

18:28.360 --> 18:32.360
You know what'll happen if that goat butts against anything? Bluey.

18:32.360 --> 18:35.360
You know what'll happen if he butts against you with all that alcohol in you?

18:35.360 --> 18:43.360
You'll both blow up.

18:43.360 --> 18:45.360
What are we gonna do, Andy?

18:45.360 --> 18:49.360
I don't know. Just... just easy. Easy. Just take it easy.

18:49.360 --> 18:52.360
How are we gonna calm him down? Look at him. He's liable to charge this desk any minute.

18:52.360 --> 18:54.360
Just... just stay calm, Warren. Stay calm.

18:54.360 --> 18:58.360
Darn that stupid goat for coming in here in the first place.

18:58.360 --> 19:01.360
If we ever get out of this alive, I'm gonna take that Cy Hudson's personally and I'm gonna...

19:01.360 --> 19:03.360
Hey, wait a minute. Wait a minute.

19:03.360 --> 19:08.360
Have you got your French harp on you? Huh? Have you got your French harp on you?

19:08.360 --> 19:10.360
At a time like this, you want me to play the French horn?

19:10.360 --> 19:13.360
You've got your French harp on you, ain't you?

19:13.360 --> 19:16.360
Yeah. Good, good. Play.

19:16.360 --> 19:18.360
Play? Play.

19:18.360 --> 19:22.360
Andy, you're having a spasm.

19:22.360 --> 19:23.360
Well, just play.

19:23.360 --> 19:30.360
Play the one you've been practicing on. Play.

19:30.360 --> 19:33.360
Good.

19:33.360 --> 19:36.360
Keep playing. Keep playing, Warren.

19:36.360 --> 19:38.360
Just keep playing.

19:38.360 --> 19:40.360
See there?

19:40.360 --> 19:43.360
You don't look so mad anymore.

19:43.360 --> 19:44.360
Andy, what are you trying to...

19:44.360 --> 19:47.360
Keep playing.

19:47.360 --> 19:49.360
Ease down off the desk.

19:49.360 --> 19:51.360
Ease down.

19:51.360 --> 19:56.360
That's right.

19:56.360 --> 20:01.360
Keep playing.

20:01.360 --> 20:04.360
Now, work your way to the door.

20:04.360 --> 20:05.360
That's right.

20:05.360 --> 20:10.360
That's good. That's good.

20:10.360 --> 20:13.360
Now, here we go.

20:13.360 --> 20:15.360
Now start walking.

20:15.360 --> 20:18.360
Play good. Play extra good.

20:18.360 --> 20:47.360
The only lego man in history is the first man to ever leave a loaded build out of time.

20:47.360 --> 20:49.360
Watch it, Barney.

20:49.360 --> 21:16.360
A clinker might set him off.

21:16.360 --> 21:27.360
You want to get that stuff together in there, Barney?

21:27.360 --> 21:28.360
Sir?

21:28.360 --> 21:30.360
Get me Mr. Burton over to Blastie.

21:30.360 --> 21:32.360
I sure am glad it's over.

21:32.360 --> 21:33.360
I'll play it out.

21:33.360 --> 21:39.360
Yeah, it's probably the first time a deputy ever got chapped lips in the line of duty.

21:39.360 --> 21:44.360
Mr. Burton, Sheriff Taylor, you can start up your Blastie again.

21:44.360 --> 21:49.360
Yeah, we got Jimmy staked out in a nice field way out of town.

21:49.360 --> 21:51.360
Yeah, I'm sure he'll be fine.

21:51.360 --> 21:53.360
Munch Blast.

21:53.360 --> 21:56.360
Right, bye.

21:56.360 --> 21:58.360
Be a nice fellow.

21:58.360 --> 22:08.360
Might as well get this stuff out of here.

22:08.360 --> 22:09.360
Yes.

22:09.360 --> 22:10.360
Yes, hush.

22:10.360 --> 22:14.360
And I'll just stand by here in case any official calls come in while they're gone.

22:14.360 --> 22:29.360
Well, I sure hope nothing happens to him.

22:29.360 --> 22:33.360
I suppose that was... was...

22:33.360 --> 22:35.360
It could only be them.

22:35.360 --> 22:55.360
They've stopped Blastie on the highway.

22:55.360 --> 22:57.360
It was them.

22:57.360 --> 22:59.360
Both of them.

22:59.360 --> 23:03.360
Snuffed out just like that.

23:03.360 --> 23:05.360
Probably Jimmy too.

23:05.360 --> 23:11.360
Two brave, brave public servants who gave their all in the line of duty.

23:11.360 --> 23:15.360
Oh, I don't deny we had our differences.

23:15.360 --> 23:20.360
But nobody can doubt that Sheriff Andrew Taylor was a fine man.

23:20.360 --> 23:24.360
Courageous, loyal, dedicated.

23:24.360 --> 23:27.360
Little fella was nice too.

23:27.360 --> 23:37.360
Yes. Deputy Fife will also go down in the annals of Mayberry history as a man of unswerving devotion to duty.

23:37.360 --> 23:43.360
Of unchallenged character, of the highest ideals.

23:43.360 --> 23:46.360
What more can I say?

23:46.360 --> 23:50.360
What more?

23:50.360 --> 23:56.360
Uh, well...

23:56.360 --> 24:01.360
You want to run through that part again about being loyal and courageous?

24:01.360 --> 24:06.360
Speak out about my unchallenged character.

24:06.360 --> 24:35.360
Much obliged, Mayor.

25:06.360 --> 25:11.360
.

